Yo, alright, alright! Let me scope out these tests and figure out what we need, man. We're not gonna overcomplicate this - just what the tests want, nothing more. That's the system, yo!

*cracks knuckles*

Looking at shopping cart tests... we need items, quantities, totals. Classic stuff. Here's the implementation that'll make everything pass:

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
	Name     string
	Price    float64
	Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
	items map[string]*Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{
		items: make(map[string]*Item),
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(name string, price float64, quantity int) {
	if existing, ok := c.items[name]; ok {
		existing.Quantity += quantity
	} else {
		c.items[name] = &Item{
			Name:     name,
			Price:    price,
			Quantity: quantity,
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(name string) {
	delete(c.items, name)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) UpdateQuantity(name string, quantity int) {
	if item, ok := c.items[name]; ok {
		if quantity <= 0 {
			delete(c.items, name)
		} else {
			item.Quantity = quantity
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItem(name string) *Item {
	return c.items[name]
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []*Item {
	result := make([]*Item, 0, len(c.items))
	for _, item := range c.items {
		result = append(result, item)
	}
	return result
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItemCount() int {
	var count int
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = make(map[string]*Item)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) IsEmpty() bool {
	return len(c.items) == 0
}
```

Yeah, orchestration! The system works, man!

Look, here's what I built - nothing fancy, just what we need:

- **NewShoppingCart** - creates an empty cart with a map for items
- **AddItem** - adds new items or bumps quantity if it exists already
- **RemoveItem** - deletes items completely
- **UpdateQuantity** - changes quantity, removes if zero or negative
- **GetItem/GetItems** - retrieves one or all items
- **GetTotal** - price × quantity for everything
- **GetItemCount** - total items including quantities
- **Clear** - empties the whole cart
- **IsEmpty** - checks if cart's empty

We're all in this together, man. I didn't add any extra validation or error handling that wasn't tested for. No checking for negative prices, no concurrent access protection, none of that. The tests didn't ask for it, so we don't build it. That's TDD, yo!

The map uses item name as the key - simple, clean, gets the job done. Tests pass, code's minimal, we're good to go!
